## Before you power anything

- Verify wiring against `include/rivet_config.h`. Every pin number came from the plan's pin
  map. Rivet's API did not choose them, and nobody has checked them against your board.
- Motor current must go through a motor driver, never through ESP32 pins.
- Supervise the rover and keep a way to cut motor power. The sketch also has a serial
  command: send `x` to DISABLE immediately, `g` to enable.
- The rover starts **disabled** at boot (`RIVET_START_ENABLED 0`).
- The distance sensor needs calibration on your hardware. A missing sensor reading makes
  the rover stop.

## Behavior

FORWARD until the front distance is below `RIVET_OBSTACLE_STOP_MM`, then STOP, then TURN for
`RIVET_TURN_DURATION_MS`, then FORWARD again. The browser simulation approximates this
policy. It does not run this code and does not prove real-world behavior.

## Build

Install PlatformIO, then run `pio run` in this folder. Library and platform versions are pinned
in `platformio.ini` but are only known to work if `compile_status` is "passed".
